ame Cc1\r\nSYMATTR Value 470p\r\nSYMBOL npn 448 416 M0\r\nWINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Q7\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N3904\r\nSYMBOL res 1200 96 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RE6\r\nSYMATTR Value 200\r\nSYMBOL pnp 1152 304 M180\r\nWINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Q6\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N3906\r\nSYMBOL cap 1072 256 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 -8 24 Right 2\r\nWINDOW 3 -8 48 Right 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Cc2\r\nSYMATTR Value 470p\r\nSYMBOL npn 1152 416 R0\r\nWINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Q8\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N3904\r\nSYMBOL Stability\\\\DiffLoopProbe 1536 576 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP1\r\nSYMBOL cap 1744 432 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 36 40 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 36 64 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName CLp\r\nSYMATTR Value 10p\r\nSYMBOL cap 1744 720 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 36 40 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 36 64 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName CLn\r\nSYMATTR Value 10p\r\nSYMBOL res 1840 432 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Rcp\r\nSYMATTR Value 100k\r\nSYMBOL res 1840 608 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Rcn\r\nSYMATTR Value 100k\r\nSYMBOL Stability\\\\LoopProbe 1952 576 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP2\r\nSYMBOL pnp 2000 624 M180\r\nWINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Q9\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N3906\r\nSYMBOL pnp 2256 624 R180\r\nWINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Q10\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N3906\r\nSYMBOL res 2144 544 R180\r\nSYMATTR InstName RT2\r\nSYMATTR Value 4.3k\r\nSYMBOL npn 2256 704 M0\r\nWINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Q11\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N3904\r\nSYMBOL voltage 2368 560 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Vcm\r\nSYMATTR Value PULSE(0 10m 0.5u 10n 10n 2u 4u)\r\nSYMBOL voltage 176 880 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName VCC\r\nSYMATTR Value 5\r\nSYMBOL voltage 320 880 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName VEE\r\nSYMATTR Value -5\r\nTEXT 176 -176 Left 2 ;NPN: 2N3904   PNP: 2N3906\r\nTEXT 736 -96 Left 2 ;Stage 1\r\nTEXT 320 -96 Left 2 ;Stage 2\r\nTEXT 1120 -96 Left 2 ;Stage 2\r\nTEXT 2000 384 Left 2 ;CMFB\r\nTEXT 1440 384 Left 2 ;Loop probe and load\r\nTEXT -64 1072 Left 2 ;A 10 mV step in Vcm, the CMFB reference: both outputs follow it together. The probes are transparent here.\r\nTEXT 176 1128 Left 2 !.tran 4u\r\n",
  "sha256:191133d49565bafb4b7b541178f48464dd245f84bacf4d56d03143aa71a0eff3": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 680\r\nWIRE -64 32 -64 16\r\nWIRE -64 16 16 16\r\nWIRE 96 16 208 16\r\nWIRE 160 16 160 -64\r\nWIRE 160 -64 304 -64\r\nWIRE 304 80 240 80\r\nWIRE 240 80 240 128\r\nWIRE -64 112 -64 128\r\nWIRE 416 48 480 48\r\nWIRE 384 -64 480 -64\r\nWIRE 480 -64 480 48\r\nWIRE 480 48 544 48\r\nWIRE 544 48 544 64\r\nWIRE 544 144 544 160\r\nFLAG 240 128 0\r\nFLAG -64 128 0\r\nFLAG 544 160 0\r\nFLAG 544 48 out\r\nFLAG 160 16 err\r\nSYMBOL voltage -64 16 M0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value AC 1\r\nSYMBOL res 112 0 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 400 -80 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R2\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 528 48 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL\r\nSYMATTR Value 2k\r\nSYMBOL ProbeCircuit 256 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP1\r\nSYMBOL TCLib\\\\OA_param 496 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 -113 80 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 -176 32 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 123 -176 48 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 39 -176 64 Left 0\r\nSYMATTR InstName U1\r\nSYMATTR Value Av=1Meg\r\nSYMATTR Value2 f1=10\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine f2=1Meg\r\nTEXT -64 560 Left 2 ;Double-click LP1 to see its circuit: ProbeCircuit is the LoopProbe (library/sub/Stability/LoopProbe.lib) drawn as a subcircuit of this project. In series in the loop,\\nVprb (an ammeter) goes from p1 to node x, Vinj (a series voltage) from x to p2 and Iinj (a current from ground) into x.\\nAll are 0 outside .stb: the probe is a wire. The .stb turns off every other AC source and runs two ac: run 1 with Vinj = 1, run 3 with Iinj = 1. With Vy = -V(x) and Iy = I(Vprb):\\n   D = Vy1·Iy3 - Vy3·Iy1        Aβ(Tian) = 1/(Vy1 + Iy3 - 2·D) - 1, T = -Aβ        R(GFT) = 1/(1/D - 1)\\nTian: the two injections (series voltage and shunt current) cancel the loading of the cut on both sides, so T does not depend on the impedances there\\nnor on the probe orientation. It is what Spectre stb computes. GFT (Middlebrook): the same two runs read as a null double injection; it treats the reverse\\ntransmission across the cut as load and, with an input and an output (gft V1 V(out)), gives G = G∞·R/(1+R) + G0/(1+R). Both give the same closed-loop poles (zeros of 1 + Aβ = 1 + R).\\nSources: M. Tian, V. Visvanathan, J. Hantgan and K. Kundert, \"Striving for small-signal stability\", IEEE Circuits and Devices Magazine 17(1), 2001.\\nR. D. Middlebrook, \"The general feedback theorem: a final solution for feedback systems\", IEEE Microwave Magazine 7(2), 2006.\\nSPICE implementations: Frank Wiedmann, https://sites.google.com/site/frankwiedmann/loopgain . More in docs/estabilidad.md.\r\nTEXT -64 832 Left 2 ;.stb LP1 dec 50 10 100meg\r\n",
  "sha256:61c1b4338e69ad571187763c96941ced3f6e1e6efc958480c415b9dfc0a56840": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 800 400\r\nWIRE 0 112 192 112\r\nWIRE 96 176 192 176\r\nWIRE 288 112 352 112\r\nWIRE 352 112 416 112\r\nWIRE 288 176 336 176\r\nFLAG 0 192 0\r\nFLAG 96 256 0\r\nFLAG 192 112 p\r\nFLAG 192 176 n\r\nFLAG 352 112 d\r\nFLAG 288 176 c\r\nFLAG 416 192 0\r\nFLAG 336 256 0\r\nSYMBOL voltage 0 96 M0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Vp\r\nSYMATTR Value SINE(1 0.5 1k)\r\nSYMBOL voltage 96 160 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Vn\r\nSYMATTR Value SINE(1 0.5 1k 0 0 120)\r\nSYMBOL BalunCircuit 240 144 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName B1\r\nSYMBOL res 320 160 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Rc\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 400 96 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Rd\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nTEXT -64 320 Left 2 ;Double-click B1 to see its circuit (BalunCircuit: the Stability > Balun drawn as a subcircuit of this project). An ideal balun with controlled sources. Ec, Ep and En build V(p) = V(c) + V(d)/2 and V(n) = V(c) - V(d)/2; Vsp and Vsn measure I(p) and I(n)\\nand the F sources put them back on the mode side as I(d) = (I(p) - I(n))/2 and I(c) = I(p) + I(n). Then V(p)·I(p) + V(n)·I(n) = V(d)·I(d) + V(c)·I(c):\\nit conserves power, so it neither isolates nor loads, and unlike a transformer it passes DC. Here Vp and Vn are 120° apart: d is their difference and c their mean (1 V with a 0.25 V ripple).\\nA DiffLoopProbe is two baluns back to back (a direct connection) with a LoopProbe on d and another on c: the .stb injects in one of them, so it cuts only one mode.\r\nTEXT -64 448 Left 2 !.tran 3m\r\n",
